id: pm-brief-0qj6
title: Adopt pm-cli 2026.11.24 host-aligned SDK behaviour
description: "Companion item pm-cli-website-spus. Migrate the published toolchain past 2026.11.14 and preserve brief rendering, output-file receipts and write ordering under the native host contract."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-brief#232",sdk
created_at: "2026-11-24T04:47:50.735Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T07:11:21.269Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Pin every first-party toolchain dev dependency to npm latest; retain structured output and file persistence guarantees in real non-Git trackers; keep typed refusals before writes; retain dependency bullets at every changelog entry point; run unchanged release, coverage, identity and changelog gates"
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T04:48:03.304Z",codex-agent,"Starting the 2026.11.23 host migration in a dedicated branch. The earlier option-contract chore covered the 2026.11.14 migration. The current npm latest pins are pm-cli 2026.11.23, pm-changelog 2026.11.20 and pm-ops 2026.11.22. Reproducing the upgraded host failures before changing assertions."
  "2026-11-24T04:51:53.534Z",codex-agent,"Dependabot baseline reports six failing top-level tests: acceptance matrix, budget write ordering, nested focus, handoff refusals, structured host output, and runtime role semantics. The host now rejects undeclared options before handlers and requires an explicit repeatable declaration for arrays. The nested focus refusal also reproduced on npm latest. Preserve document, file, budget and lifecycle assertions while exercising declared per-command options and asserting the old accidental options are refused."
  "2026-11-24T04:51:59.342Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed upstream pm-cli#1775 directly on 2026.11.23. Reproduce with scanMutationSecrets(JSON.stringify({ title: [\"api\",\"key\"].join(\"_\") + \": \" + String.fromCharCode(36) + \"{API_KEY}\", updated: \"2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z\" })); the reference-only title returns rule credential_key_assignment and should return an empty result. The package continues to use the native scanner."
  "2026-11-24T05:04:18.510Z",codex-agent,"The host now rejects undeclared options before handlers. Prompt uses its own governance threshold and fixed format; handoff show takes an ID and receiver; next accepts neither governance controls nor days; structured read fixtures now supply flags per command. Explicit refusals, budget and no-write checks stay in place. Shared focus declares repeatable and retains both native selectors. Reverting the focus declaration or changelog flag fails those tests. The targeted command run passed 8/8; typecheck, build, the 200-declaration docstring gate and isolated strict health passed. Changelog regeneration kept all 12 published dependency bullets and restores 37 historical bullets."
  "2026-11-24T05:26:18.509Z",codex-agent,"The linked seven-file regression run passed 357/357 tests with zero failures, cancellations or skips. It exercised the installed brief, command rendering, output files, native tracker operations and host refusals. npm and Bun release gates will run with unchanged thresholds against the final commit. Upstream pm-cli#1775 remains open."
  "2026-11-24T07:11:19.482Z",codex-agent,"The baseline reproduced exactly six host failures among 639 tests. The intermediate npm release gate passed 641/641 with 98.05 percent branch coverage and all seven packed scenarios. The global and ephemeral scenarios picked up npm latest 2026.11.24 during validation and passed. Refresh the dependency pin to that version, then rerun both release gates. The same reference-only scanner finding remains on 2026.11.24."
